  "notes": "1980s-facing synth-pop with maximal hook density. The drums are the entry's: \"gated 1980s snare on 2&4, four-square kick, tambourine on offbeats, and a synth-generated 8th pulse in place of hats; drum fills are tom cascades.\" So the snare is hard-transient under a large tail, `hihat.base` is 8th with no roll vocabulary, `tambourine` sits at `offbeat` placement, and the fills are `tom`/`tomHigh`/`tomLow` with the snare-roll ladder off. The bass is explicitly not an 808: \"pumping analogue-style synth bass on 8ths with an octave jump per bar\", which is `offbeat_8ths` with an octave in the cell shapes — the \"1—8\" figure is the octave jump the entry names. Harmony is \"bright majors with a borrowed minor iv and a IV—V—vi—I lift habit\", so that lift is a named family and the borrowed iv is the `borrowed` map. The melody block is where this model earns its separation: \"toplines are hook-dense — pre-chorus, chorus and post-chorus each carry a distinct singable figure\", so `densityPerBar` runs 6—13, the arrangement authors a post-chorus-shaped structure with three separate hook slots, and \"contour is ascending and wide, with breathy doubles\" is the arch weighting, the high `octaveJumpProb` and the `octave_echo` counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says the parameters are \"lane-derived\": every drum probability, the humanize pair, the melody register, `bpm.mode` 120 (the midpoint of the stated 110—130 band) and the `lydian` weight in `session.scales` are INFERRED — the entry says \"bright majors with a borrowed minor iv\" and names no mode, so lydian is an inferred bright colour at weight 2. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the soprano-placement claim is repeated here.",
